---
// Conceptual sketch of the COMPASS idea. Not data: no values are taken from the paper.
---

<figure class="concept">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 560 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="cf-title cf-desc">
    <title id="cf-title">Conceptual sketch of the COMPASS signal</title>
    <desc id="cf-desc">
      Two curves show how much a model's output changes as Gaussian noise added to an image grows. At low noise the curve for
      training images stays below the curve for unseen images; the shaded low-noise band marks where the gap is largest.
    </desc>
    <rect x="70" y="20" width="120" height="180" class="band" />
    <text x="130" y="38" class="lbl band-lbl" text-anchor="middle">low-noise regime</text>
    <line x1="60" y1="200" x2="540" y2="200" class="axis" />
    <line x1="60" y1="200" x2="60" y2="20" class="axis" />
    <path d="M 62 196 C 120 190, 170 175, 230 140 S 380 60, 530 42" class="curve non" />
    <path d="M 62 198 C 120 196, 170 190, 230 162 S 380 72, 530 48" class="curve mem" />
    <text x="300" y="232" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle">noise level σ added to the image →</text>
    <text x="22" y="110" class="lbl" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-90 22 110)">change in model output →</text>
    <g class="legend" transform="translate(360 150)">
      <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="22" y2="0" class="curve non" />
      <text x="30" y="4" class="lbl">unseen images</text>
      <line x1="0" y1="22" x2="22" y2="22" class="curve mem" />
      <text x="30" y="26" class="lbl">training images</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="small muted">
    Conceptual sketch, not results. In many settings, images a model was trained on respond less to small amounts of noise
    than unseen images do. COMPASS finds the noise level and the direction of this gap from unlabeled data.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .concept { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }
  svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .axis { stroke: var(--faint); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .band { fill: var(--accent-soft); }
  .curve { fill: none; stroke-width: 2.4; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .curve.non { stroke: var(--faint); stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }
  .curve.mem { stroke: var(--accent); }
  .lbl { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; fill: var(--muted); }
  .band-lbl { fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 11px; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.6rem; }
</style>
